    crm:P3_has_note "Arrangement Journals, letters, and sketchbooks are arranged roughly in sequential number sequences, housed in document boxes.",
        "Bibliography Leisten, Thomas, 2003: \"Excavation of Samarra, v. I. Architecture : Final report of the first campaign 1910-1912. Verlag Philipp von Zabern, Mainz am Rhein, 2003.\"",
        "Date/Time and Place of an Event Note Notes related primarly to the first campaign of excavation at Sāmarrāʼ (Iraq), carried out by Ernst Herzfeld on behalf of the Kaiser Friedrich Museum in Berlin in 1911.",
        "General - Series title in Joseph Upton's Catalogue of the Herzfeld Archive reads, \"Records of Samarra Expeditions.\"",
        "General - Title is provided by Xavier Courouble,FSg Archives cataloger, based on Joseph Upton's Catalogue of the Herzfeld Archive Joseph Upton's Catalogue of the Herzfeld Archive and Thomas Leisten's publication, Excavation of Samarra, vol 1.",
        "Local Numbers S-4:6 FSA A.06 07.04.6",
        "Scope and Contents - Additional information reads, \"Only the payroll booklet of the first campaign is preserved in the Sackler Archives. From this material it becomes clear that normally one crew of workers consisted of 20-25 men led by a foreman. For most of the time Herzfeld tried to maintain seven crews. After he had lost at least 50% of his workers in late spring and summer 1911, his efforts to make up the losses can be seen from the payroll of August 30, 1911. His workforce had expanded to 9 crews with most of them having 27-29 men. From a note in one of the letters to Sarre we learn that the normal working day lasted 10 hours. Only during Ramadan was the time reduced to 9 hours; see AP IV, Letter of August 5. 1911.\" [Leisten, Thomas, 2003: \"Excavation of Samarra, v. I. Architecture : Final report of the first campaign 1910-1912. Verlag Philipp von Zabern, Mainz am Rhein, 2003. p. 15.\"]",
        "Scope and Contents - Finding aid title reads, \"Workmen's payroll, Samarra January 9, 1911 - August 30, 1911.\" [Joseph M. Upton's Catalogue of the Herzfeld Archive, compiled in 1974]" ;
    crm:P48_has_preferred_identifier kg:id_ark_ref24608 ;
