    crm:P3_has_note "Arrangement Journals, letters, and sketchbooks are arranged roughly in sequential number sequences, housed in document boxes.",
        "Date/Time and Place of an Event Note Notes related primarly to the two campaigns of excavation at Sāmarrāʼ (Iraq), carried out by Ernst Herzfeld on behalf of the Kaiser Friedrich Museum in Berlin between the years 1911 and 1913.",
        "Funding note Funded by",
        "General - Series title in Joseph Upton's Catalogue of the Herzfeld Archive reads, \"Records of Samarra Expeditions.\"",
        "General - Since these are primary sources, handwritten captions in the sketchbook are specified in three stages: (1) an English designation following Thomas Leisten and Alastair Northedge's terminology; (2) the transcribed original caption in German which is provided under parenthesis; and (3) additonal information from Herzfeld's publication, \"Der Wandschmuck der Bauten von Samarra und Seine Ornamentik. Verlag Dietrich Reimer, Ernst Vohsen, Berlin, 1923.\" and Thomas Leisten's publication, \"Excavation of Samarra, v. I. Architecture : Final report of the first campaign 1910-1912. Verlag Philipp von Zabern, Mainz am Rhein, 2003\" which is provided under bracket.",
        "General - Title is provided by Xavier Courouble, FSg Archives cataloger, based on Joseph Upton's Catalogue of the Herzfeld Archive.",
        "Local Numbers S-24 FSA A.06 07.24",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten caption on cover reads, \"Samarra ; plan aufnahmen 4.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten notes for pg. 1 and 2reads, \"Topographical measurements including Balkuwārā (Manqūr).\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten notes for pg. 11 and 12 reads, \"Topographical measurements.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten notes for pg. 13 and 14 reads, \"Topographical measurements; [Balkuwārā palace, general plan of the complex with outer enclosure].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten notes for pg. 15 and 16 reads, \"[Balkuwārā palace, gate I, sketch of southern wing]; [Balkuwārā palace, gate I, sketch of southern wing]; [Balkuwārā palace, ornament 24]; [Balkuwārā palace, gate III].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten notes for pg. 17 and 18 reads, \"[Balkuwārā palace, southwest quadrant of the palace]; [Balkuwārā palace, southwest quadrant of the palace].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten notes for pg. 19 and 20 reads, \"[Balkuwārā palace, Great (eastern) Īwān]; [Balkuwārā palace, Great (eastern) Īwān].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten notes for pg. 21 and 22 reads, \"[Balkuwārā palace, Great Īwān, horizontal timber-frame construction]; [Balkuwārā palace, Great Īwān, vertical timber-frame construction].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten notes for pg. 23 and 24 reads, \"[Balkuwārā palace, wall enclosure around courtyard I and including gate I]; [Balkuwārā palace, Great (eastern) Īwān].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten notes for pg. 25 and 26 reads, \"[Balkuwārā palace, Great (eastern) Īwān]; [Balkuwārā palace, bath].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten notes for pg. 27 and 28 reads, \"[Balkuwārā palace, Mosque I]; [Balkuwārā palace, bath, soffit of arch in the alcove vaults].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten notes for pg. 29 and 30 reads, \"[Balkuwārā palace, bath]; [Balkuwārā palace, Great (eastern) Īwān].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten notes for pg. 3 and 4 reads, \"Topographical measurements.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten notes for pg. 31 and 32 reads, \"[Balkuwārā palace, Great Īwān, blind niches]; [Balkuwārā palace, bath, ornament 1b]; [Balkuwārā palace, courtyard III].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten notes for pg. 33 and 34 reads, \"[Balkuwārā palace, River Garden, pavilion A]; [Balkuwārā palace, vertical timber-frame construction].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten notes for pg. 35 and 36 reads, \"[Balkuwārā palace]; [Balkuwārā palace, Mosque I].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten notes for pg. 37 and 38 reads, \"[Balkuwārā palace, gate III]; [Balkuwārā palace, niches in room 7 and 9].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten notes for pg. 39 and 40 reads, \"--; --; [Qubbat al-Ṣulaibiyya]; --; [Balkuwārā palace, ornament 1b].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten notes for pg. 41 and 42 reads, \"[Balkuwārā palace, ornament 28 and 29]; [Balkuwārā palace, niches in room 7 and 9]; [Qubbat al-Ṣulaibiyya, inscription I].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten notes for pg. 43 and 44 reads, \"[Qubbat al-Ṣulaibiyya, octagonal building]; [Qubbat al-Ṣulaibiyya]; [Qubbat al-Ṣulaibiyya, octagonal building]; [Qubbat al-Ṣulaibiyya, inscription II].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten notes for pg. 45 and 46 reads, \"[House XI (formerly Haus VII)].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten notes for pg. 5 and 6 reads, \"Topographical measurements.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten notes for pg. 7 and 8 reads, \"Topographical measurements.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten notes for pg. 9 and 10 reads, \"Topographical measurements.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - The thirteenth of a series of eighteen sketchbooks (Skizzenbücher), in which Ernst Herzfeld recorded his observations on topography, landscape, archaeological remains, architecture, artifacts and decorative motifs, related to the congregational mosques in Samarra, Mutawakkiliyya, and Balkuwārā; the Qubbat al-Ṣulaibiyya; the palaces of Balkuwārā, Ṣūr ʿĪṣā, and the Qaṣr al-ʿĀshiq; and finally the residential architecture and the baths at Quraina, Wadī al-Muḥḥ, Qāṭūn, Jubairiyya, and west of Ṣūr ʿĪṣā.",
        "Scope and Contents Excavation of Samarra (Iraq): Architectural Studies 4" ;
